<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hugh-de-lacy-earl-of-ulster"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/hugh-de-lacy-earl-of-ulster.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hugh de Lacy, Earl of Ulster</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hugh de Lacy, a younger son of the Lord of Meath, was made Earl of Ulster by King John in 1205 after he had driven out John de Courcy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hugh-de-lacy-lord-of-meath"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/hugh-de-lacy-lord-of-meath.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hugh de Lacy, Lord of Meath</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hugh de Lacy was an Anglo-Norman baron who in 1172 received from Henry II the former Kingdom of Mide as the Lordship of Meath, to balance Strongbow's power in Leinster.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hugh-ii-of-jaffa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/hugh-ii-of-jaffa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hugh II of Jaffa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hugh II of Le Puiset (c. 1106–1134) was Count of Jaffa in the Kingdom of Jerusalem and a cousin of Queen Melisende.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hugh-iii-duke-of-burgundy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/hugh-iii-duke-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hugh III, Duke of Burgundy</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hugh III was duke of Burgundy from 1162 to 1192.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hugh-iv-duke-of-burgundy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/hugh-iv-duke-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" hei